/-!
# Polynomial Gamma bounds and two-prime Weil decomposition at aperture `log 2`

At aperture `A = log 2` (lag diameter `2 * log 2 < 7 / 5`), the degree-fourteen
Gamma lower kernel loses roughly `10⁻⁷` near the window boundary, exceeding the
ground-energy scale `1.70 × 10⁻¹⁰` of the two-prime Weil form. This module
establishes:

1. A degree-22 polynomial lower bound `retainedGammaPolyRem` for
   `retainedGammaRemainderWeight` on `(0, 7 / 5]`, combining the degree-22
   reciprocal `sinh` Taylor polynomial with a degree-11 Chebyshev lower
   polynomial for `1 / cosh` certified by exact rational sum-of-squares and
   homogeneous Bernstein decompositions.
2. A matching upper kernel bound `archLevySinhWeight_le_poly14_cosh26` on
   `(0, 7 / 5]` with uniform pointwise error at most `4 / 10¹⁰`, used to certify
   the sharp upper bound on `ccmRestrictedWeilGroundEnergy ⟨log 2, _⟩`.
3. The exact two-prime Weil decomposition `weilQuad_two_prime_decomposition` at
   aperture `log 2` (using continuity at boundary lag `log 4 = 2 * log 2` to
   eliminate `n = 4`) and the degree-14 comparison functional
   `twoPrimeDegree14GammaForm ≤ weilQuad`.
-/

noncomputable section
open Real MeasureTheory Set Filter Topology Zeta23
open _root_.RHTower _root_.RHTower.ArchimedeanAnomaly
open _root_.RHTower.WeilMarkovPole _root_.RHTower.WeilLevyPoleGauss
